      {
        "introduction": "Using three allegories, God foretells Judah's imminent destruction. The first allegory shows Judah as a useless vine to be burned. The second is a vitriolic attack against Judah's unfaithfulness, portraying Judah as an adulterous wife, worse than her two sisters, Israel and Edom, and less moral than a prostitute. The third allegory, using two eagles and a vine, calls specific attention to the personal ruin of King Zedekiah."
